window.docContents[174].resolve({"/Output-Formats/#output-html":{"contents":"While most users of Verso don't need to worry about the specific details of the HTML that it produces, authors of new genres or of substantial extensions to existing genres may need to produce custom HTML.\nVerso's HTML output follows a number of conventions and uses built-in libraries and features.\n\nLean's Html type represents HTML documents.\n\nHTML content, which may be either a single node or a sequence of sibling nodes.This type is optimized for convenient authoring of HTML documents.\nIt is not formally related to\nthe HTML DOM representation.\nIt is analogous to React's Fragment.An element with the given tag name, attributes, and children.Textual content.The characters &, <, and > are always escaped to HTML entities during rendering.\nUse raw\nin raw text elements\n(script and style) instead.Characters to be copied verbatim (and not escaped) during rendering.A sequence of HTML values.\n\nEmpty HTML.\n\nMerges an array of HTML values by appending them.Like seq, but may produce a more compact representation.\n\nMerges a list of HTML values by appending them.Like seq hs.toArray, but may produce a more compact representation.\n\nAppends two HTML forests.\n\nRewrites the forest by using fn to transform every node.\nTraversal proceeds in post-order:\nfn receives element and seq nodes with already-rewritten children.\n\nRenders into a string to be consumed by browsers.\nThe input's structure is respected as much as possible:* No whitespace is added or removed.* Tag names are not escaped.The output uses HTML5 syntax.\nIt is not compatible with XML syntax for HTML.Details of the output syntaxWe make the following XML-compatible choices:* Void elements with isEmpty children are rendered as self-closing tags.* Void elements with non-isEmpty children are rendered like normal elements.\nSuch elements are forbidden by the HTML spec.* Attribute values are always double-quoted.And the following incompatible choices:* Attributes with empty values are minimized.\n\nHTML documents are typically produced using an embedded DSL, accessible via the html%{…} literal syntax.\nFor example, this definition creates a <ul> list:\n\ndef mkList (xs : List Html) : Html :=\n  html%{<ul>{ xs.map fun x => html%{<li>{x}</li>} }</ul>}\n\n#eval mkList [\"A\", html%{<emph>B</emph>}, \"C\"]\n  |>.render\n  |> IO.println\n\n\n<ul><li>A</li><li><emph>B</emph></li><li>C</li></ul>\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Writing Documentation in Lean with Verso\u0009Output Formats","header":"5.1. HTML","id":"/Output-Formats/#output-html"}});